    "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base",
    "problem": "Given that $y=5{log}_{4}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
    "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
